    "text_1883190477": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "jcr:created": "Thu Aug 15 2024 18:58:57 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h2>Stryker leadership reflects on the value of a diverse workplace</h2>\n<p>After the 2024 Summit, Stryker leaders have been sharing insights on the transformative power of a diverse workplace. &quot;At the end of the day, DE&amp;I is about being a good human,” says Annie Heath. “This means caring for each other, speaking up for those who may not feel they have a voice and recognizing that small steps can add up to big strides.&quot;</p>\n<p>Andy Pierce, Group President, MedSurg and Neurotechnology – also the executive sponsor for SOMOS, our ERG dedicated to the Hispanic/Latino community – shared in his closing remarks: &quot;Be an ally and a champion for others. You can change your perspective through small actions. Empathy is a bridge to acceptance.&quot;</p>\n<p>Our President of Asia Pacific, John Collings shared, “True DE&amp;I goes beyond policies and workshops. It is about creating and fostering a culture where every individual feels safe and included. When we start to embrace true DE&amp;I, we start to foster an environment where everyone can thrive.”</p>\n<p>By understanding each other’s “why,” we cultivate a culture where everyone feels seen, heard and valued. In a recap video, employees summed up our fourth-annual Summit best: “As we return to our daily lives, our work, our communities, friends and teams, we carry with us a piece of every person we have met, enriched by their stories and inspired by their “why.”</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Aug 15 2024 19:26:37 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "bottomMargin": "3",
